ent-ClothingNeckCape = cape
    .desc = A beautiful, flowing cape. Too bad it tangles too much on the vegetation.

ent-ClothingNeckShortCloak = ladylike shortcloak
    .desc = Ermine trimmed, handed down.

ent-ClothingNeckForestCloak = forrester cloak
    .desc = A cloak worn by the Black Oaks of Azuria.

ent-ClothingNeckBearCloak = direbear cloak
    .desc = Made from the finest, warmest bear pelt. It might be worth more than your life.

ent-ClothingNeckDupatta = dupatta
    .desc = A regional variant of the humble sash, loosely fit to fight against the Ranesheni heat.

ent-ClothingNeckPoncho = cloth poncho
    .desc = A loose garment that is usually draped across ones upper body. No one's quite sure of its cultural origin.

ent-ClothingNeckRainCloak = rain cloak
    .desc = This one will help against the rainy weather.

ent-ClothingNeckScoutCloak = scout cloak
    .desc = A weathered cape cut short at the flank.

ent-ClothingNeckShadowcloak = stalker cloak
    .desc = A heavy leather cloak held together by a gilded pin, depicting the Grand Duke's house. The sign of a faithful servant.

ent-ClothingNeckThiefcloak = rapscallion's shawl
    .desc = A simple shawl clapsed with an ersatz fastener. Practical and functional, though the fabric is rough and wearing bare.

ent-ClothingNeckToga = toga
    .desc = The ancestral predecessor to Psydonia's many tabards, worn by the townsfolk, heroes, and villains of antiquity.

ent-ClothingNeckTribal = tribal pelt
    .desc = A haphazardly cured pelt of a creecher, thrown on top of one's body or armor, to serve as additional protection against the cold. Itchy.

ent-ClothingNeckWardencloak = warden's cloak
    .desc = A cloak of dense, thick wool worn by the Wardens of Azuria's Forests. Incredibly warm, and doubles as a blanket in a pinch.

ent-ClothingNeckWickerCloak = wicker cloak
    .desc = A makeshift cloak constructed with mud, sticks and fibers.

ent-ClothingNeckHalfCloak = half cloak
    .desc = A short travelling cloak draped over one shoulder.

ent-ClothingNeckSnowCloak = snow cloak
    .desc = A cloak meant to keep one's body warm in the cold of the mountains as well as the dampness of Azuria.
